| Game for Mupen64Plus: run by the launcher (!RunImage) with a ROM's name (Unix form) to play it
| in a desktop window. Arguments go to mupen64plus. Settings and saves are in
| <Choices$Write>.Mupen64Plus; its output goes to stdout and stderr there.
| RISC OS port of Mupen64Plus. Copyright (C) 2026 David Sharp. GPL-2.0.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.03 RMLoad <Mupen64Plus$Dir>.PThrTicker
RMEnsure RISC3D 0.05 Error Mupen64Plus needs !RISC3D (RISC3D 0.05 or later) in !Boot.Resources, to draw with OpenGL

| Sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager if they're in !System; silent without them.
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| Settings and saves; the defaults the first time.
CDir <Choices$Write>.Mupen64Plus
CDir <Choices$Write>.Mupen64Plus.Saves
IfThere <Choices$Write>.Mupen64Plus.mupen64plus/cfg Then Set Mupen64Plus$Choices yes Else Copy <Mupen64Plus$Dir>.Defaults.mupen64plus/cfg <Choices$Write>.Mupen64Plus.mupen64plus/cfg ~C~V
CDir <Mupen64Plus$Dir>.Screenshots
| UnixLib's names with a system variable in them, set without expanding it (|<)
Set XDG_DATA_HOME /|<Choices$Write>/Mupen64Plus
Set XDG_CACHE_HOME /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>

| Test hooks' variables (src/n64_check.c) left over from a test run would change how it runs.
Unset N64_*
| The launcher's icon stays on the icon bar for the game (its menu has the game's commands), so
| the emulator puts none of its own there; its commands come through Mupen64Plus$Command.
Set Mupen64Plus$LauncherIcon 1
Unset Mupen64Plus$Command
WimpSlot -min 200000K -max 200000K
Run <Mupen64Plus$Dir>.Mupen64 --configdir /<Choices$Write>/Mupen64Plus %*0 >/<Choices$Write>/Mupen64Plus/stdout 2>/<Choices$Write>/Mupen64Plus/stderr
Unset Mupen64Plus$LauncherIcon
